    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12977" root="دلك" body-key="d">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَلَكٌ</span></b>  The <i>time of the setting of the sun:</i> or <i>of
its declining from the meridian:</i> one says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَتَيْتُكَ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عِنْدَالدَّلَكِ</span>, meaning <i>I came to thee in the evening,</i>
or <i>afternoon.</i> (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  Also <i>A looseness,</i> or
<i>laxness, in-the knees</i> of a camel. (Sgh, K.)

